      "title": "Chapter 5: Proofs, Pitfalls and Real Choices",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "title": "Case Study: Three Salary Structures, Three Take-Home Outcomes",
          "slug": "case-study-three-salary-structures-three-take-home-outcomes",
          "body": [
            {
              "_key": "k1",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Three people, three cities, three very different CTCs. Aditi earns ₹14 lakh, Rakesh ₹28 lakh and Sameer ₹45 lakh. Each has built the right structure for their own life, and each ends up in a different regime with a very different share of CTC landing in the bank.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k3",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k4",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "This final lesson runs all three end to end, using every rule from the course, and then hands the method back to you.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "bigIdea",
              "text": "There is no best salary structure. There is only the structure that fits your rent, your family, your regime and your stage of life.",
              "_key": "k5"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k6",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k7",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Case 1: Aditi, 26, Bengaluru, ₹14 lakh CTC",
